= Slippage — Simple =

Slippage is the difference between the price you expected for a trade and the price you actually received. It can come from changing markets, thin liquidity, delays, or your trade's effect on the market. A slippage-tolerance setting is only a limit, not the actual slippage.

'''Important boundary:''' slippage ≠ price impact.

